1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,170
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:05,180
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

4
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:06,440
(Episode 8)

5
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:13,350
I just bought this,

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,720
and I barely used it. What is this?

7
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:17,420
It is completely shattered.

8
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,430
This is so upsetting.

9
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:23,030
I should have gotten
that crazy jerk's name.

10
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,430
Why didn't I think of that?

11
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,300
I am the CEO's daughter
of this company.

12
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,540
This is when I should have
really thrown my weight around.

13
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:37,880
Do Yun.

14
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,880
You know what?
Mom cut my credit card limit in half.

15
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,510
How petty of her.

16
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:45,020
So I came to complain, but you know,
she is not in her office.

17
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,420
So, you know,
I was wondering if you...

18
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:50,490
Seriously.
Stop saying "you know" all the time.

19
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:53,190
She's not here,
and she's busy, Se Na.

20
00:00:57,030 --> 00:00:58,560
Do Yun, what is wrong?

21
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:03,170
I feel so wronged and uneasy
that I can't take it.

22
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:04,900
About what?

23
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,280
Swipe it all you want.
Right, just for this month.

24
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:15,110
Really?

25
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:16,980
Can I really swipe it
as much as I want?

26
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:19,450
- But in return, you...
- Yes, Do Yun.

27
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:21,690
Come somewhere with me later.

28
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:23,460
Where are we going, Do Yun?

29
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,340
Gang Nam.

30
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,210
What is it, Mom?
Do you need my help?

31
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,340
About Mi Seon...

32
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,410
Didn't she have quite a few friends?

33
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,750
Yes, she has a few.

34
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,350
Did you go see them?

35
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:59,260
With her pride,

36
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,990
she would never contact her friends,

37
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:04,600
and she definitely
would not go see them.

38
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,870
I know her best.

39
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,070
If you know her so well,
why did this happen?

40
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,100
You should have treated her better.

41
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,310
Mom.

42
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:24,180
When Su Ah's mom and I came out
of the courthouse for the last time,

43
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,850
the weather was so sunny.

44
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:30,960
There was a park
right next to the courthouse.

45
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:36,460
So we each bought a cup of coffee...

46
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:39,960
and sat together on a park bench
to talk for a bit.

47
00:02:43,570 --> 00:02:45,300
It had been a really long time...

48
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:48,210
since we had done that
just the two of us.

49
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,410
But it was
on the day of our divorce.

50
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:57,920
Yes. It is funny.

51
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:01,920
What did you talk about?

52
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:06,720
Not much, really.

53
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:10,160
She did most of the talking.

54
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:13,800
What could I possibly say?

55
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,000
I just kept crying.

56
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,470
I don't even remember
exactly what she said,

57
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:21,640
but in the end,

58
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,440
she said...

59
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,610
to stop crying.

60
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,180
And to stop worrying about her.

61
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,050
She said she wasn't a tree,
but grass.

62
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:38,560
A weed, specifically.

63
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,090
If a tree...

64
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:43,760
gets hit hard
by a typhoon or lightning,

65
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:45,730
it can break in one strike.

66
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,500
But she said a weed...

67
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,240
will keep coming back to life,
no matter how much...

68
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,170
it's trampled and crushed.
Something like that.

69
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:58,910
I mean, I don't know where
she picks up things like that.

70
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,850
And as she left,

71
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:11,160
I couldn't even lift my head.

72
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,200
My tears and snot kept running.

73
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:19,900
Goodness.

74
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,370
It was really...

75
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:24,540
embarrassing...

76
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:29,410
as a man or as a human being.

77
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:35,080
Goodness.

78
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,280
Now...

79
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,520
I really have to let her go.

80
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:51,030
That was the only thought I had.

81
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:57,000
Quit acting cool
and come inside, you rascal.

82
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,500
What?

83
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:05,510
You still have to eat, right?
And I have to feed you.

84
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,590
Right...

85
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,320
I still have to eat.

86
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:36,270
Thank you again for today, sir.
Take care.

87
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:37,910
Have a good day.

88
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,480
Yes, thank you, sir.

89
00:05:40,550 --> 00:05:43,050
- Always drive safely.
- Yes, I will.

90
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,660
My gosh.

91
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:04,670
Even people who live
in places like this...

92
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,400
must have at least one worry, right?

93
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,110
Would it be just one?

94
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:11,810
If you have a lot of money,
you get dozens of problems.

95
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,980
Right.
It's not like I have never had it.

96
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,780
- Yes.
- Hello.

97
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,550
Gosh, right.

98
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:25,360
- Did you call for me?
- I'm alone.

99
00:06:25,590 --> 00:06:27,860
- You can relax.
- Yes, ma'am.

100
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:44,140
Here's the information you requested
of that incident.

101
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,980
I reached out to the people
involved in the investigation...

102
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,280
as secretly as possible.

103
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,720
I think it would be best for you,
Madam Chairwoman,

104
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:52,580
to read it yourself
and make a judgment.

105
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:55,990
I only provided the money.

106
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:59,890
Dr. Ju, you must have gone
through a lot of trouble.

107
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,230
It took longer than expected.

108
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,360
There are still
more things to verify,

109
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:07,300
and there is still more evidence
to find.

110
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:11,170
If I were alone,
I would not have made it this far.

111
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,510
Dr. Ju.

112
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:18,040
Yes, please speak.

113
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:20,850
Do you think our Seung Yun...

114
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,780
left for the US...

115
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:26,920
just because he wanted
to study design?

116
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:32,460
That boy left
to build up his strength.

117
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,590
It worries me.

118
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,700
The boy who was a gentle sheep...

119
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,800
will return as a tiger,

120
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,770
so one day, there will be
a huge uproar in this family.

121
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:49,940
I must prevent that boy
from getting hurt again.

122
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,510
Please keep helping me
just like you are now.

123
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,710
Yes, Madam Chairwoman.

124
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,480
Yes.

125
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:03,790
(CEO Cha In Sung)

126
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:04,960
Yes.

127
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:07,430
(Hwanggeum Capital)

128
00:08:08,430 --> 00:08:09,430
Gosh, honey.

129
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,030
What brings you here
without calling?

130
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:14,800
I had an outside meeting nearby.

131
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,400
I stopped by for a bit
because I missed you,

132
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:20,100
- are you very busy?
- Oh, no matter how busy I am,

133
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:23,880
when my lovely wife comes to visit,
I have to put everything aside.

134
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,080
Come sit down, honey.

135
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:31,680
Oh, by the way.

136
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:34,250
I still can't reach Seung Yun.

137
00:08:34,950 --> 00:08:36,650
Is he not answering
your calls either?

138
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:40,320
Now that he is all grown up,

139
00:08:40,590 --> 00:08:42,830
it makes me sad that he seems
to forget sometimes...

140
00:08:42,830 --> 00:08:44,100
how much we care about him.

141
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,200
Oh my.

142
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,060
Do you feel that way too?

143
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:50,100
I thought I was the only one
who felt sad.

144
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:57,170
- Yes?
- Madam Chairwoman,

145
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:01,310
do you think Seung Yun
figured something out...

146
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:02,950
on his own and left?

147
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,880
He was a young boy
when he left for the US.

148
00:09:06,950 --> 00:09:11,760
Seung Yun was very mature,
even as a young boy.

149
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:15,630
When he lost his parents
in that accident back then,

150
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,000
he barely survived.

151
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:21,170
After he was discharged
from the hospital,

152
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:24,800
that boy never once spoke a word
about his parents' deaths...

153
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:26,470
or about what happened that day.

154
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:30,210
He never spoke a word about it,

155
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:33,810
as if nothing had happened.

156
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:37,680
To me, that has always been...

157
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,120
a thorn in my side.

158
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,350
Yes?

159
00:09:46,590 --> 00:09:48,630
- All right.
- Yes, ma'am.

160
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,370
Goodness.

161
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,710
Oh, that's okay.

162
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,140
- Thank you so much.
- Gosh.

163
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:09,310
You are giving me
this much of a tip?

164
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:12,280
You brought me home safely, right?

165
00:10:12,350 --> 00:10:13,380
It is just a token
of my appreciation.

166
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:14,820
I would appreciate it
if you accepted it, sir.

167
00:10:14,890 --> 00:10:16,250
Yes, thank you, then.

168
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:20,290
- Have a good day.
- Yes.

169
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:38,040
Goodness, I'm really back home.

170
00:10:48,550 --> 00:10:49,550
Seung Yun?

171
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:54,360
- Seung Yun!
- Hey.

172
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:56,890
It's been so long! I missed you.

173
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,860
Hey, come on. I can't breathe.

174
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:01,900
Seriously, what is wrong with you?

175
00:11:01,970 --> 00:11:03,700
Se Na, since the last time
I saw you,

176
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:06,870
- What?
- you've gained some weight.

177
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,340
- What?
- No, you got a little older.

178
00:11:09,410 --> 00:11:11,710
Are you going to be like this
as soon as we meet?

179
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:12,780
I am joking.

180
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,940
Let's go inside now.
Is Grandma home?

181
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:15,010
Yes.

182
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:19,180
Wait, who is here?

183
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,190
Are you saying our Seung Yun
is really here?

184
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,850
Yes, madam.

185
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,560
It looks like he is coming in
with Se Na.

186
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,160
Oh my.

187
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:32,560
- Gosh.
- Grandma, look who's here.

188
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:34,670
It's the one you've been waiting for,
going on and on about...

189
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:35,800
how much you missed him.

190
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:37,130
Oh, my.

191
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:40,940
- Oh, my...
- Grandma, I'm here.

192
00:11:41,010 --> 00:11:44,140
Oh, yes, my baby. Goodness.

193
00:11:44,210 --> 00:11:46,210
You must be exhausted
from the long trip.

194
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:47,910
My goodness.

195
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:49,150
Oh, yes.

196
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:51,520
Goodness.

197
00:11:59,590 --> 00:12:00,690
My goodness.

198
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:17,110
There, there.

199
00:12:17,170 --> 00:12:18,180
Goodness.

200
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:22,350
Yes, sit down.

201
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,920
Oh, my.

202
00:12:29,050 --> 00:12:30,050
What?

203
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,360
There we go.

204
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:42,800
Mrs. Ma abandoned me
to get remarried.

205
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,700
She should have learned
her lesson...

206
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:47,370
after suffering so much
the first time.

207
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:49,740
Why try to change her destiny
at that age?

208
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,240
Her destiny was ruined
from the start,

209
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:54,580
so I doubt her later years
would be any different.

210
00:12:58,050 --> 00:13:00,080
She has only been here
for a few days.

211
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,550
She says her hometown is Anseong.

212
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,990
I look forward to your help, ma'am.

213
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,660
I have heard a lot about you.
You must be tired. Please have some.

214
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:14,800
Madam, I'll go prepare dinner now.

215
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:17,130
Please call me if you need anything.

216
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,200
Go about your work.

217
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,940
- Have some tea.
- Yes.

218
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,180
Our Grandma is
perfectly lucid today.

219
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:33,320
Did you not see Dr. Ju visit?

220
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:36,320
Maybe it is because I took
the new medicine he prescribed.

221
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,190
Could changing your medicine
really make you lucid right away?

222
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:43,790
Seung Yun just picked a good day
to come back home.

223
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:46,260
You've already given Grandma
a formal bow.

224
00:13:46,330 --> 00:13:48,400
Let's see the gifts you got
for the family.

225
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:53,370
Gosh, right. I am sorry, Grandma.

226
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:56,170
What? For what?

227
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:59,510
That floral scarf you asked me
to buy for you.

228
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:01,050
I couldn't get it. I am sorry.

229
00:14:01,310 --> 00:14:02,880
But if you wait just a little bit,

230
00:14:02,950 --> 00:14:05,420
I will find an even prettier one
for you.

231
00:14:08,290 --> 00:14:12,220
Wait, when did I ever
ask you for a scarf?

232
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,790
When we talked on the phone
last time, you asked for a scarf...

233
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:21,070
I told you she forgets sometimes,
so just let it go.

234
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,300
There is nothing to worry about,
Seung Yun.

235
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:30,370
Your Grandma is perfectly fine.

236
00:14:41,590 --> 00:14:42,590
Se Na.

237
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,530
Is Grandma's condition
getting worse?

238
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:52,730
It is bad when it's bad.
But when she's fine,

239
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,600
she's completely normal,
as if nothing was ever an issue.

240
00:14:55,970 --> 00:14:57,470
Really?

241
00:14:57,530 --> 00:14:59,040
And this Dr. Ju,

242
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,600
do you think his skills
are reliable?

243
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:05,140
Outpatient treatment might be better
at a university hospital instead.

244
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:09,210
Grandma insists on
only being treated by Dr. Ju.

245
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,710
Mom and Dad have completely...

246
00:15:10,710 --> 00:15:12,820
given up because of
Grandma's stubbornness.

247
00:15:15,550 --> 00:15:17,120
- Seung Yun.
- Yes?

248
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:19,660
I had a favor to ask you
when you came back.

249
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:20,760
Will you hear me out?

250
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:22,490
What is it?

251
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:26,630
I want to launch
my own underwear brand,

252
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:29,170
but no one in our family
will listen to me.

253
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:33,500
Mom even drastically reduced
the limit on my credit card.

254
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:38,410
Take a look at my designs first
and be my first investor.

255
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:40,240
I heard you made a lot of money.

256
00:15:40,310 --> 00:15:41,780
I heard everything
Mom and Dad were saying.

257
00:15:43,210 --> 00:15:45,920
All right, bring them to me later.
I will take a look and decide.

258
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,450
I knew it.

259
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,150
I knew you would be on my side.

260
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,350
Thank you, Seung Yun.

261
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,420
I never said I would help you.

262
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:34,100
I'm sorry, Grandma.

263
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:45,480
Hey, Danny.

264
00:16:46,110 --> 00:16:47,210
I just got home.

265
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:49,110
Your Grandma must be
so happy to see you.

266
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,280
Since you are back home,

267
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:54,280
take some time off
and find some girls, my boss.

268
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,790
Everything is good to go.
So please relax.

269
00:16:58,090 --> 00:17:00,060
I'm always on your side, Seung Yun.

270
00:17:00,590 --> 00:17:02,890
Thanks. I will get back to you soon.

271
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,400
What does he want me to do?

272
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:24,080
If you don't mind,
could I get your number?

273
00:17:26,020 --> 00:17:28,550
That might be difficult, sir.

274
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,550
Personal meetings with customers...

275
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:33,690
are strictly prohibited
under our VIP service policy.

276
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:37,530
Dating is out of the question.

277
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:50,440
Thank you for coming.

278
00:17:50,910 --> 00:17:52,010
Please, go ahead.

279
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,680
It's a completely
different world here.

280
00:17:56,550 --> 00:17:58,550
I have never seen
such a pretty coffee cup, Da Mi.

281
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:01,550
Do people who come
to places like this...

282
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,350
have an easier life?

283
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,290
I don't think
that is necessarily true.

284
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,560
For example?

285
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,590
I would love to hear about it.

286
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:13,100
I can't leak
customers' personal information.

287
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:15,270
You don't want me
to lose my job, do you?

288
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:17,200
Goodness. Of course not.

289
00:18:23,810 --> 00:18:26,340
This is delicious.
Coffee made by someone else...

290
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:28,210
is always the best in the world.

291
00:18:28,350 --> 00:18:31,010
Just like ramyeon and rice.

292
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:35,250
Su Ah is doing well
and staying healthy.

293
00:18:36,190 --> 00:18:38,590
Why don't you ask about her
when you miss her so much?

294
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,830
As a mom who abandoned
her own child,

295
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,130
do I even have the right to ask?

296
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:47,430
I just feel sorry for your mother.

297
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:51,100
By the way,
why did you ask me to come?

298
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:54,870
I heard your new rooftop apartment
had no deposit,

299
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:56,810
but the rent was
800 dollars a month.

300
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:03,710
This is 10,000 dollars.

301
00:19:03,710 --> 00:19:06,380
Use this as a deposit
and lower your rent even a little bit.

302
00:19:09,390 --> 00:19:10,790
Da Mi.

303
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:12,690
Why? Are you that surprised...

304
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:14,790
that a cheapskate like me
has this kind of money?

305
00:19:16,330 --> 00:19:17,730
That's part of it, but I...

306
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,500
can't accept this money.

307
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,170
I'm in no position
to pay you back every month,

308
00:19:23,570 --> 00:19:25,240
and I can't even promise...

309
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:27,500
when I'll be able to.

310
00:19:28,410 --> 00:19:31,640
I'm not lending it to you.
I'm just giving it to you.

311
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,980
Please just take it, Mi Seon.

312
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:39,150
Actually, ever since I heard about
your divorce from Gang Nam,

313
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:41,720
I've felt so sorry for you.

314
00:19:42,850 --> 00:19:43,850
When things were tough,

315
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:46,120
I couldn't even
help you out properly,

316
00:19:46,990 --> 00:19:50,660
and on your birthday,
I never even gave you a proper gift.

317
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:55,500
You always gave everything
to our family.

318
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:58,570
Thank you.

319
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:01,970
I know you worked hard
to save this money.

320
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,580
How is the new job you just got?

321
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:09,950
I've only been there a few days,
so what can I really say?

322
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:13,580
I just have to grit my teeth
and keep going.

323
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:15,920
I work three shifts,
so it's a bit tiring,

324
00:20:15,990 --> 00:20:17,450
but these days,
for women with career breaks like me,

325
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,520
finding a job is nearly impossible.

326
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:21,390
Oh, I almost forgot.

327
00:20:22,890 --> 00:20:25,430
Please give this to your mother.
I bought it on my way here.

328
00:20:26,530 --> 00:20:27,900
Is it skincare?

329
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,800
It's nothing expensive.

330
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:32,940
Her face and hands get so dry,

331
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,910
and I figured
she was probably running out.

332
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:39,880
I'll make sure she gets it.

333
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,750
- That hurts, Do Yun.
- Hurry up.

334
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:49,190
I should get going, Da Mi.

335
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,950
I'll call you later.
Get home safely.

336
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:52,760
Who exactly are you
trying to meet here...

337
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:54,960
Welcome, sir.

338
00:20:55,030 --> 00:20:56,990
- Do you have a reservation?
- No.

339
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:01,470
Why is that pervert here again?
Oh, boy.

340
00:21:01,530 --> 00:21:03,930
You actually have a girlfriend, sir?

341
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:06,070
Right now, Manager Kang,

342
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,870
you're wondering why
that pervert showed up again.

343
00:21:09,110 --> 00:21:10,610
And you're thinking
I somehow have a girlfriend,

344
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:11,680
are you not?

345
00:21:12,010 --> 00:21:13,580
How did you...

346
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,080
Not at all, sir.

347
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:21,920
I was just thinking how nice it was
that you decided to visit us again.

348
00:21:21,990 --> 00:21:24,990
I felt so wronged and uncomfortable
about what happened...

349
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,990
that I just had to come
clarify things,

350
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,730
which is why I'm here.

351
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:30,290
Let's sit down for a moment.

352
00:21:30,490 --> 00:21:31,730
Right, right this way.

353
00:21:33,530 --> 00:21:34,770
What are you standing around for?

354
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:36,570
- Hurry up.
- Okay.

355
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,480
First of all,
about what happened that day.

356
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:49,210
Whatever do you mean, sir?

357
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,820
I'm talking about
the unfortunate incident...

358
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:58,090
involving those hideous items
that came out of my jacket pocket.

359
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,530
By hideous items,

360
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:06,300
are you referring to
that provocative bra and thong?

361
00:22:07,430 --> 00:22:09,300
Why are they hideous to you?

362
00:22:10,170 --> 00:22:13,700
Are you disparaging
women's underwear right now?

363
00:22:13,770 --> 00:22:15,070
That is not what I meant.

364
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,010
Just stay quiet.

365
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:22,710
I am not the kind of person
you think I am.

366
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:25,550
All right? I am not a pervert.

367
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:28,090
You really didn't seem
to believe me,

368
00:22:28,150 --> 00:22:30,790
so I made a point to bring
my younger sister here today.

369
00:22:30,990 --> 00:22:33,790
I had no idea you were
worrying about that so much.

370
00:22:34,730 --> 00:22:37,690
So, you are saying this is
your younger sister?

371
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:42,230
Hey, what are you doing?

372
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,600
Hurry up and answer.

373
00:22:44,870 --> 00:22:46,400
You just told me to stay quiet.

374
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:49,910
I'll cancel the credit card.

375
00:22:50,170 --> 00:22:52,010
I'll answer if you let me use it
for three months.

376
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:00,380
Yes, I am his younger sister.

377
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:04,250
I put the underwear I designed
into his jacket pocket...

378
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:05,590
as a joke back then.

379
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:07,990
I got in a lot of trouble for it.

380
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:10,630
I heard he was completely
humiliated here.

381
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,730
So please clear up
the misunderstanding.

382
00:23:15,730 --> 00:23:17,370
I had already forgotten about it.

383
00:23:18,370 --> 00:23:20,870
You didn't need to go
to such lengths, sir.

384
00:23:21,340 --> 00:23:23,140
I fully understand the situation.

385
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:25,380
Please don't worry about it anymore.

386
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,880
I'm fine, really.

387
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:30,350
Excuse me?

388
00:23:31,210 --> 00:23:33,820
Yes, well, if you say so,
I understand.

389
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:37,890
But did you say you designed
the underwear yourself?

390
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:38,890
Yes.

391
00:23:38,890 --> 00:23:41,290
This might be a rude question,

392
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,690
but do you work
for an underwear brand?

393
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,830
No.

394
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,660
But why do you ask?

395
00:23:47,730 --> 00:23:50,530
The design was really pretty,
so it stuck in my memory.

396
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:51,840
The colors were great, too.

397
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,500
Really?

398
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,640
Actually, my dream is
to be a designer too,

399
00:23:56,710 --> 00:23:58,280
so I practice in my spare time.

400
00:23:59,040 --> 00:24:01,380
I was even wondering
which brand it was from.

401
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:06,220
So, Manager Kang, your dream is
to be a designer too.

402
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:10,090
In clothing, right?
Womenswear or menswear?

403
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:12,690
I would love to see
what you have designed sometime.

404
00:24:12,760 --> 00:24:13,790
Hey, get up.

405
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:16,560
Let's go home.

406
00:24:16,630 --> 00:24:19,900
Why?
We are having a conversation here.

407
00:24:20,430 --> 00:24:21,500
You go first.

408
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:23,330
Are you kidding me?

409
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:28,510
Well, we will be leaving now.

410
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:33,510
See you later, Manager Kang.
I will come by again.

411
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:37,480
Thank you, sir.
Have a safe trip back.

412
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:44,050
How distracting.

413
00:24:52,930 --> 00:24:53,930
It's so hot.

414
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:02,940
Su Ah, don't you get sick
of those ice pops?

415
00:25:03,170 --> 00:25:05,710
There are so many kinds
of ice cream in the world,

416
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:07,540
so why do you always pick this one?

417
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:11,110
You know,
humans should pursue diversity.

418
00:25:11,180 --> 00:25:13,780
You have to experience
a wide variety of things...

419
00:25:13,850 --> 00:25:16,190
to find the path
that is just right for you...

420
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:17,850
and push forward to the end.

421
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:20,520
You tried a wide variety
of businesses...

422
00:25:20,590 --> 00:25:22,090
and went completely bankrupt, Dad.

423
00:25:23,190 --> 00:25:27,100
What? Who said that?
Who said I went completely bankrupt?

424
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:30,370
Mom did, and so did
Great-Grandma and Grandma.

425
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:33,970
Great-Aunt, too.

426
00:25:34,040 --> 00:25:37,810
- Also...
- Okay, stop.

427
00:25:39,010 --> 00:25:41,080
Gosh, they're adults,

428
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:44,250
but they don't filter what they say
in front of a growing child.

429
00:25:45,420 --> 00:25:48,920
And they said a person
has to dig one well to succeed.

430
00:25:49,750 --> 00:25:51,890
What? Who said that?

431
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:53,260
Great-Grandma did.

432
00:25:55,290 --> 00:25:59,400
Gosh, that is because Great-Grandma
is from the older generation.

433
00:25:59,900 --> 00:26:02,730
In an AI world like today,
my daughter,

434
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,830
it's...

435
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,740
Gosh, that's not necessarily true.

436
00:26:08,810 --> 00:26:10,340
Mom said that...

437
00:26:10,340 --> 00:26:13,740
what the elders say
is never wrong, Dad.

438
00:26:14,510 --> 00:26:18,180
Gosh, they brainwashed her.
They really brainwashed her.

439
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:21,380
- Dad.
- Yes.

440
00:26:21,450 --> 00:26:23,890
From now on, when you come
to pick me up, wash your face.

441
00:26:23,950 --> 00:26:25,560
And shave, too.

442
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:28,960
Mom always looked pretty
when she came.

443
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:35,770
Okay. I'm sorry.

444
00:26:46,180 --> 00:26:49,510
- Excuse me.
- Yes. Thank you. Please come again.

445
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:50,580
The food was great.

446
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,780
What can I get for you?

447
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:55,350
Oh, it's not that.

448
00:26:55,420 --> 00:26:58,290
It's our first time here today,
and it's so delicious.

449
00:26:58,360 --> 00:26:59,690
I want to take some to my kids.

450
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:02,530
Please pack two orders of
Ginseng Chicken Soup for me.

451
00:27:02,590 --> 00:27:04,030
- It's your first time?
- Yes.

452
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:05,300
- It is delicious, right?
- Yes.

453
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,700
Once you eat here,
you can't eat anywhere else.

454
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:07,730
Tell me about it.

455
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:08,930
I'll get them ready for you to take.

456
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,000
- Thank you.
- Okay.

457
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:14,070
Boss, we have two to-go orders
of Ginseng Chicken Soup.

458
00:27:14,140 --> 00:27:15,240
Okay.

459
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:22,780
Oh, Mother.
I told you to go inside and rest.

460
00:27:23,050 --> 00:27:25,380
We won't have
any more dinner customers. Okay?

461
00:27:26,220 --> 00:27:29,820
Why is Dae Chi not going to work
and staying here all day?

462
00:27:31,520 --> 00:27:34,490
Yes, about that, Mother.

463
00:27:35,130 --> 00:27:36,890
He said he took a few days off.

464
00:27:37,430 --> 00:27:39,360
He has not had a day off in a while.

465
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:43,200
If he wants to rest,
he should rest at his own house.

466
00:27:43,470 --> 00:27:46,540
Why is he lying around here all day?

467
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,360
(Mission: Mompossible)

468
00:28:10,690 --> 00:28:13,060
Lend your brother some money.

469
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:14,900
Dae Chi is also...

470
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:16,330
Did I cause a financial accident?

471
00:28:16,430 --> 00:28:18,940
Why are you taking
all your anger out on me?

472
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:20,940
You like Manager Kang,
don't you, Do Yun?

473
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,040
Me?

474
00:28:22,110 --> 00:28:25,780
Put your hand over your heart.
I bet your heart is beating fast.

475
00:28:26,980 --> 00:28:28,980
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
